WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.307 --> 00:00:18.511
again Zann found himself plummeting through a shadowy kaleidoscope of colors and shapes.

2
00:00:19.291 --> 00:00:22.634
This time, though, Wyssa wasn't there to steady or guide him.

3
00:00:23.554 --> 00:00:26.777
As he felt Perda's hand slipping from his arm, he panicked.

4
00:00:27.737 --> 00:00:32.965
Then he realized the magical shackles were still in place, binding him and Perda together.

5
00:00:32.985 --> 00:00:35.707
"Is everyone still here?"

6
00:00:36.087 --> 00:00:37.908
he shouted, struggling to look back.

7
00:00:38.768 --> 00:00:41.050
The movement sent him flying in a new direction.

8
00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.092
But he could see his friends strung out behind him.

9
00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:49.015
Perda and Gliss were clinging to each other, while Darb hung onto Gliss' legs.

10
00:00:49.835 --> 00:00:52.397
Zing was clutching Zann's backpack with his claws.

11
00:00:52.877 --> 00:00:54.438
Everyone looked terrified.

12
00:00:55.078 --> 00:00:56.519
Zann tried to gather his thoughts.

13
00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:57.660
It wasn't easy.

14
00:00:58.388 --> 00:01:01.490
His trip through the vortex with Wyssa had been overwhelming enough.

15
00:01:02.451 --> 00:01:04.592
This was much, much worse.

16
00:01:05.833 --> 00:01:10.316
Countless wormholes slid past, offering glimpses into other worlds.

17
00:01:11.297 --> 00:01:13.538
How had Wyssa pulled them through one of them?

18
00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:15.420
Zann struggled to remember.

19
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.302
"Zann!" Darb's voice sounded faint and frightened.

20
00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.143
"What do we do now?"

21
00:01:21.964 --> 00:01:24.205
Zann lunged for the next wormhole they passed.

22
00:01:24.986 --> 00:01:26.327
His friends were counting on him.

23
00:01:26.347 --> 00:01:30.601
"Oof!" His fingers grasped only empty air.

24
00:01:31.362 --> 00:01:33.503
The effort sent the entire group spinning.

25
00:01:33.783 --> 00:01:34.944
Gliss let out a shriek.

26
00:01:34.964 --> 00:01:36.444
"Hold on!"

27
00:01:36.745 --> 00:01:37.365
Darb shouted.

28
00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:39.606
"Is everyone okay?"

29
00:01:40.187 --> 00:01:40.767
Zann yelled.

30
00:01:41.427 --> 00:01:45.830
He could feel Perda's arm shackled to his, and Zing's hot breath on his neck.

31
00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:47.851
Were the other two still with them?

32
00:01:47.871 --> 00:01:49.632
"We're okay!"

33
00:01:50.252 --> 00:01:51.333
Gliss sounded breathless.

34
00:01:51.353 --> 00:01:55.315
"I—I don't know how much longer we can hold on though!"

35
00:01:56.375 --> 00:01:57.116
Zann gulped.

36
00:01:57.504 --> 00:01:58.585
He had to get them out of here!

37
00:01:59.425 --> 00:02:03.248
More worlds slid by, but Zann was unable to reach any of them.

38
00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:10.333
It was a struggle merely staying conscious and alert; with every passing moment, he could feel more energy

39
00:02:10.393 --> 00:02:11.393
draining from him.

40
00:02:12.694 --> 00:02:17.597
Soon he felt as if even a simple Door-opening spell would be more than he could manage.

41
00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:21.520
Would he and his friends end up spinning through the vortex forever?

42
00:02:22.361 --> 00:02:27.244
Like Morb, like poor Venna under the Dousing spell, like Zann's parents?

43
00:02:28.252 --> 00:02:29.893
"We have to do something!"

44
00:02:30.254 --> 00:02:30.834
Perda cried.

45
00:02:30.854 --> 00:02:32.075
"I know."

46
00:02:32.535 --> 00:02:36.538
Even pushing out the words took almost more energy than Zann had left.

47
00:02:36.558 --> 00:02:42.262
"I just don't—" Suddenly Zing whistled eagerly in his ear.

48
00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:48.706
Another wormhole was sliding past; this one revealed a large fish leaping out of the water.

49
00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:55.250
Zing lunged, stretching out with his front claws while keeping his hind claws in Zann's backpack.

50
00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.352
"Zing!" Darb cried.

51
00:02:57.708 --> 00:02:59.709
"This is no time to think about food!"

52
00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:03.352
But somehow Zing was clawing at the edge of the wormhole.

53
00:03:04.513 --> 00:03:09.736
Zann felt a strong sucking sensation, as if his entire body were being compressed.

54
00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.118
"Wait!" Gliss cried.

55
00:03:12.138 --> 00:03:16.121
"I'm losing hold of Perda—" Splash!

56
00:03:16.961 --> 00:03:19.243
Zann plunged into a gray sea.

57
00:03:20.164 --> 00:03:22.865
Its waves grabbed him, flipping him head over heels.

58
00:03:23.666 --> 00:03:26.408
It was almost as disorienting as being in the vortex.

59
00:03:27.812 --> 00:03:31.435
Zann was so tired that he wasn't sure he could fight the angry water.

60
00:03:32.176 --> 00:03:37.941
He was tempted to give up, let himself sink beneath the waves forever Then he felt a yank

61
00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:38.521
on his arm.

62
00:03:39.362 --> 00:03:44.246
A moment later his head popped above the surface and he gulped in cool, moist air.

63
00:03:45.247 --> 00:03:48.189
Perda was bobbing beside him, panting with exhaustion.

64
00:03:48.209 --> 00:03:50.471
"Where's everyone else?"

65
00:03:50.971 --> 00:03:51.452
she asked.

66
00:03:52.733 --> 00:03:54.734
Wind-driven rain made it hard to see.

67
00:03:55.255 --> 00:03:56.596
Zann blinked away the moisture.

68
00:03:57.532 --> 00:04:01.253
Zing was floating nearby, flapping his wings and looking disgusted.

69
00:04:02.213 --> 00:04:03.534
Zann almost smiled.

70
00:04:03.954 --> 00:04:05.514
The dragon wasn't a fan of swimming.

71
00:04:06.394 --> 00:04:09.095
One of Zann's favorite tricks was to dunk him in the river.

72
00:04:10.155 --> 00:04:13.796
Zann tried to focus; he realized his weary mind was wandering.

73
00:04:14.597 --> 00:04:18.778
Treading water, he turned and spotted Gliss and Darb bobbing nearby.

74
00:04:18.798 --> 00:04:21.258
"There you are!"

75
00:04:21.598 --> 00:04:22.019
he called.

76
00:04:22.759 --> 00:04:27.060
He struck out toward them but realized his arm was still attached to Perda's.

77
00:04:27.916 --> 00:04:29.337
For a moment he was annoyed.

78
00:04:30.198 --> 00:04:33.660
Then he realized that the shackles were what had saved him.

79
00:04:34.921 --> 00:04:36.282
She must have pulled him to the surface.

80
00:04:37.102 --> 00:04:40.264
By now Darb and Gliss had spotted them and were swimming over.

81
00:04:40.284 --> 00:04:43.286
"Everyone okay?"

82
00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:45.068
Darb panted.

83
00:04:45.088 --> 00:04:46.929
"I think so."

84
00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:50.952
Zann squeezed his eyes shut as a larger wave washed over them.

85
00:04:52.052 --> 00:04:55.415
He was relieved to feel his magic energy already coming back.

86
00:04:56.355 --> 00:04:59.869
He glanced at Zing, who had finally shaken off enough water to fly.

87
00:04:59.889 --> 00:05:01.730
"Go higher, boy!"

88
00:05:02.071 --> 00:05:02.671
Zann called.

89
00:05:02.691 --> 00:05:03.952
"Find land!"

90
00:05:05.953 --> 00:05:06.933
He glanced at the others.

91
00:05:06.953 --> 00:05:08.254
"Try to rest.

92
00:05:08.954 --> 00:05:13.097
Then when Zing shows us which direction to go, we can zap to land."

93
00:05:13.117 --> 00:05:15.558
"Yeah," Gliss said.

94
00:05:15.578 --> 00:05:18.139
"If our magic works in this world."

95
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:19.900
Zann gulped.

96
00:05:20.361 --> 00:05:21.281
He hadn't thought of that.

97
00:05:21.301 --> 00:05:23.222
"I'll test my magic."

98
00:05:23.683 --> 00:05:24.883
Perda touched the shackles.

99
00:05:24.903 --> 00:05:27.821
"Release!" The shackles disappeared.

100
00:05:27.841 --> 00:05:30.703
"Looks like it still works," Zann said.

101
00:05:30.723 --> 00:05:34.567
"It's weird here," Gliss said, her voice shaking.

102
00:05:35.307 --> 00:05:37.949
"The rain—it's not any color at all!

103
00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.311
Just clear!"

104
00:05:39.331 --> 00:05:42.213
"Never mind that," Perda said.

105
00:05:42.233 --> 00:05:43.594
"I'm getting tired.

106
00:05:43.674 --> 00:05:45.035
Let's make a boat or something."

107
00:05:45.936 --> 00:05:47.958
She linked hands with Zann and Gliss.

108
00:05:48.538 --> 00:05:50.420
Even combined, their energy was weak.

109
00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.582
All they could manage was a small wooden raft.

110
00:05:54.403 --> 00:05:57.029
When it was finished, Zann felt drained once again.

111
00:05:57.869 --> 00:06:00.250
Still, the raft was big enough to hold them all.

112
00:06:01.451 --> 00:06:03.371
"What's taking him so long?"

113
00:06:04.192 --> 00:06:07.433
Gliss squinted up at Zing, who was circling rapidly overhead.

114
00:06:08.273 --> 00:06:10.174
The dragon's whistle sounded uneasy.

115
00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:14.536
Suddenly Zing squawked loudly and dived toward them.

116
00:06:15.456 --> 00:06:16.197
Zann frowned.

117
00:06:16.657 --> 00:06:17.697
"What's he doing?"

118
00:06:18.057 --> 00:06:18.518
he wondered.

119
00:06:19.498 --> 00:06:23.540
At that moment something jolted the raft from below, flipping it up and over.

120
00:06:24.392 --> 00:06:28.314
Zann barely had time to gasp before he felt himself falling into the sea.

121
00:06:29.475 --> 00:06:34.298
He fought his way back to the surface just in time to see their raft being swallowed by

122
00:06:34.338 --> 00:06:37.079
a creature like none he'd ever seen before.

123
00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:45.604
It was a huge, jelly-like beast the size of the largest dragons— like an enormous jellyfish with a

124
00:06:45.724 --> 00:06:47.465
gaping, hungry mouth.

125
00:06:48.406 --> 00:06:51.108
And several more were surfacing nearby!
